f September 30, 2026, down from 14.75%/16.82% a year earlier as the balance sheet scaled.\n- Net worth has grown consistently from Rs. 15,257 crore (Mar-18) to Rs. 49,445 crore (Sep-26), with Book Value Per Share rising from Rs. 31.37 (Mar-21) to Rs. 57.34 (Sep-26), an 83% increase.\n- Articulated long-term goal of ~20% stable balance-sheet growth, GNPA below 2% and NNPA below 1%, and a 'high teens' ROE target, continuing to reinvest profits into scaling the deposit, rural and other newer businesses.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"- Built a full suite of universal banking products spanning retail lending, rural lending, SME lending, deposits, NRI banking, FASTag, trade finance, transaction banking/CMS, credit cards, treasury/forex and wealth management, alongside corporate lending.\n- Differentiates from traditional banks by using 15 years of cash-flow analysis and machine-learning/deep-learning credit scorecards to profitably underwrite self-employed, rural and micro-entrepreneur segments that traditional banks avoid.\n- Mobilised ~US$3.6 billion of FCNR(B) deposits from NRI customers despite having no branch, subsidiary or representative office outside India, demonstrating digital reach and customer trust.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Corporate history] IDFC FIRST Bank was formed via the December 2018 merger of erstwhile IDFC Bank (demerged from IDFC Limited in 2014, focused on wholesale/infrastructure lending) and Capital First (an NBFC founded 2012 focused on tech-driven retail/MSME lending), under MD & CEO V. Vaidyanathan.\n- [Regulatory commentary] Management expects the FY28 profitability impact of IRDAI's consultation paper on insurance commissions to be broadly offset by the ~1% funding-cost benefit from FCNR(B) deposit mobilisation, domestic deposit savings, product changes and an assumed 25 bps repo hike in each of FY27 and FY28.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 24-10-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"A universal bank built since the 2018 merger around 15 years of cash-flow/ML-based underwriting in underserved retail, rural and MSME segments, now scaling digital liabilities, cards and wealth management while reducing wholesale concentration.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":2.51,"fy":"FY22","mcap":24684,"opm":19.1,"pe":186.6,"roe":0.7},{"de":2.22,"fy":"FY23","mcap":36433,"opm":22.0,"pe":14.7,"roe":10.6},{"de":1.58,"fy":"FY24","mcap":53307,"opm":20.6,"pe":18.1,"roe":10.1},{"de":1.03,"fy":"FY25","mcap":40242,"opm":20.2,"pe":27.0,"roe":4.2},{"de":7.04,"fy":"FY26","mcap":60177,"opm":32.8,"pe":36.8,"roe":3.8}],"wtt":null},"drhp":{"rpt":{"financials":{"_source":"ledger","balance_sheet_key":[{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2019","total_assets_amount_rs":1670989300000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2020","total_assets_amount_rs":1491585500000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2021","total_assets_amount_rs":1630715200000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2022","total_assets_amount_rs":1901457300000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2023","total_assets_amount_rs":2398820500000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2024","total_assets_amount_rs":2962097800000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2025","total_assets_amount_rs":3439087400000},{"basis":"Consolidated","fy":"FY2026","total_assets_amount_rs":3997746400000}],"pnl_3yr":[{"basis":"Consolidated","depreciation_amount_rs":0,"finance_cost_amount_rs":0,"fy":"FY2019","other_income_amount_rs":9386400000,"tax_amount_rs":-13295500000,"total_income_amount_rs":131426600000},{"basis":"Consolidated","depreciation_amount_rs":0,"finance_cost_amount_rs":0,"fy":"FY2020","other_income_amount_rs":17224100000,"tax_amount_rs":4975000000,"total_income_amount_rs":179627300000},{"basis":"Consolidated","depreciation_amount_rs":0,"finance_cost_amount_rs"